    {
      "title": "Habitats and Ecology",
      "level": 1,
      "path": [
        "Habitats and Ecology"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Basselinia pancheri occurs in dense humid forest and secondary forests on serpentine soils derived from ultramafic rocks from sea level to 1,000 m asl. This is a solitary, rarely clustered, palm tree which grows to 15 m tall. It appears to tolerate some disturbance being often found in secondary forest or exposed sites (Dowe 1989, Hodel and Pintaud 1998)."
        },
        {
          "type": "style",
          "data": {
            "bold": [],
            "italic": [
              "Basselinia pancheri"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
